stinction, or relationship within second law and entropy. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before entropy balance because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "2463b723-174b-422b-9c2e-089c24e9ca06", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Entropy balance", "children": [], "description": "Entropy balance is a governing quantity in second law and entropy, linking local calculations to system-level behavior and offering a consistency check. After clausius inequality, entropy balance supplies what is needed to address entropy generation."}, {"id": "b61ec410-ed4a-463e-8ead-d09931847dec", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Entropy generation", "children": [], "description": "Entropy generation is a governing quantity in second law and entropy, linking local calculations to system-level behavior and offering a consistency check. As the final topic in this module, entropy generation carries the completed idea into exergy."}]}, {"id": "5f0b1d89-7c67-4cfe-81e2-f516ca956d47", "type": "topic", "title": "Exergy", "description": "This module builds directly on second law and entropy and develops exergy. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for vapor power cycles.", "children": [{"id": "631aa49b-a37d-4713-bc4e-a804cdf723b8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Useful work", "children": [], "description": "Useful work identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within exergy. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before dead state because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "4f433f6f-7453-43fc-91f1-2daece09f9a0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dead state", "children": [], "description": "Dead state identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within exergy. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After useful work, dead state supplies what is needed to address irreversibility."}, {"id": "d913f23d-ee71-4357-8d75-bec06abfa136", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Irreversibility", "children": [], "description": "Irreversibility identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within exergy. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After dead state, irreversibility supplies what is needed to address second-law efficiency."}, {"id": "304e6a78-4164-43c5-882c-67ede419aeaf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Second-law efficiency", "children": [], "description": "Second-law efficiency provides a formal guarantee or inference rule for exergy, allowing later conclusions to be justified rather than inferred from examples alone. As the final topic in this module, second-law efficiency carries the completed idea into vapor power cycles."}]}, {"id": "57161ca2-eddc-4907-b755-0b702ee764b2", "type": "topic", "title": "Vapor power cycles", "description": "This module builds directly on exergy and develops vapor power cycles. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for gas power cycles.", "children": [{"id": "f4a33f0d-ec00-40a6-bde4-8eb03dca8b54", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Rankine cycle", "children": [], "description": "Rankine cycle identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within vapor power cycles. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before reheat because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "4aa62670-84df-4ab5-bbd0-05ce04152436", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reheat", "children": [], "description": "Reheat identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within vapor power cycles. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After rankine cycle, reheat supplies what is needed to address regeneration."}, {"id": "57e58eba-e1e9-45fd-99ee-1f629c9c656f", "type": "subtopic"